{"kind":"report","text":"Formal exact-head review of the final Tailapp v1 implementation artifact c03d8bf9 at head a293f58c94c36d222002983560bffa2cdf7ac116. Verdict: approved.\n\nVerification basis: I independently checked out and verified this exact commit in a clean worktree during the advisory cycle for request #55 — go test ./..., go vet ./..., go test -race ./... over every package, and scripts/demo.sh all pass, and the worktree is byte-clean at the head. The head resolves, matches the branch tip, and the artifact citation is verbatim.\n\nThis head is the accumulation of five reviewed increments, each inspected at its exact commit: the bounded profile compiler with the fixed otlp_record -\u003e otel_event -\u003e tables topology and single-writer ownership enforced through views; the closure of the comma-join ownership evasion and JSONata wildcard nondeterminism under RuntimeID @2; durable bounded OTLP intake with byte-stable canonicalization, preserved metric temporality/monotonicity, and running capacity accounting; atomic per-record projection transactions with declared reads, aligned flat waves, and the default-deny query sandbox with export-only mounting and a deterministic runtime budget; the corrected failure model — transient-versus-deterministic error classification, per-app unavailability, journaled two-phase activation with crash reconciliation, and gap repair by boundary-resetting continuation, each pinned by a dedicated crash or cancellation test; and durable mutation idempotency with conflict and in-doubt refusals replayed across restart.\n\nAgainst the ratified notes and request #15's conditions: the complete product stands — one binary, resident engine with process lock, loopback OTLP/HTTP for logs/traces/metrics, bounded durable inbox with captured obligations, draft/validate/continue-or-reset lifecycle under CAS and idempotency keys, isolated per-app SQLite projections with exact frontiers, bounded read-only SQL through one control service with CLI and MCP parity, and recovery without duplicate interpretation. The immediate-value criterion is met honestly: the bundled agent-guard normalizes Claude Code, Codex, and OpenCode telemetry into policy findings with observed/unknown coverage that never claims compliance from absent fields, repetition/failure/no-progress loop evidence gated on observed telemetry, and caller-cutoff stall queries; session-cost joins it at query time through explicit exports; the demo proves all of it through both CLI and MCP; and the artifact text, README, and MCP tool descriptions all state plainly that these are detective controls, not inline enforcement.\n\nKnown non-blocking items carried on the record for future work, none affecting the v1 contracts: idempotency-record retention (unbounded rows at low mutation rates), the global mutation mutex spanning activation drains, the query budget's documented dependence on the pinned driver's progress-callback cadence, and the deferred-scope list ratified in the design (single event type, skip-and-count policies, tick records, replay). Milestone E harness smoke tests against live Claude Code/Codex/OpenCode exporters remain the operator's acceptance step outside this repository-scoped review.\n\nApproved at exact head a293f58c94c36d222002983560bffa2cdf7ac116.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:c03d8bf975bd200a871754faa4229e60295cc3d3","head":"a293f58c94c36d222002983560bffa2cdf7ac116","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:ce20d4c2add2f32e415500d368b55ed2e73c9ec6\",\"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:d31fbfac7737ada2a0807612d09449675589d74d\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:d31fbfac7737ada2a0807612d09449675589d74d","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}